 "drivingQuestion": "How can the mishna invalidate a side signature when Rav signed on the side?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Answered provisionally; the answer is challenged in the next unit.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "gittin.88a.5",
   "daf": "88a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "חָתְמוּ עֵדִים בְּרֹאשׁ הַדַּף וְכוּ׳. אִינִי?! וְהָא רַב חָתֵים מִן הַצַּד! הָתָם בְּשֶׁגַּגּוֹ כְּלַפֵּי כְתָב.",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna: If «the witnesses signed at the top of the column» or on the side, the bill of divorce is invalid. The Gemara raises an objection: «Is that so? Wouldn’t Rav sign on the side?» The Gemara answers: «There,» in the case of Rav, he would sign «with the roof,» i.e., the top, «of» his signature «facing the text» of the document, so it was clear that he was signing the document."
  }
